      <div class="pf-faq">
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">COST</span>&nbsp; How much does an emergency plumber cost in Southport?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>£80 an hour weekdays 9am to 5pm. £120 an hour weekends 9am to 1pm. £150 an hour out of hours, nights and bank holidays. 1 hour minimum on every call-out. Parts at cost. Same rates as our Liverpool coverage. No distance premium for Southport. Most jobs cost £80 to £350. Written quote before work starts. No call-out fee.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">RESPONSE</span>&nbsp; How quickly can you reach Southport from Kirkby?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Honest answer: 35 to 45 minutes via the A570 or A59. Southport has no direct motorway link. If you need a 15 minute response, a local Southport plumber will be faster. We're useful when the local plumbers are tied up, for out of hours cover, and for landlords with portfolios spanning Sefton.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">WHY US</span>&nbsp; Why would I call a Kirkby plumber for Southport?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Three reasons. First: when the local Southport plumbers are tied up or unavailable, we are. Second: we charge our standard rates with no Southport distance premium. Third: we cover the whole of Sefton at the same rates, so landlords with rentals in Maghull, Crosby, Formby and Southport can use one phone number.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">AREAS</span>&nbsp; Do you cover Birkdale and Ainsdale?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Birkdale (PR8 4), Ainsdale (PR8 3), Hillside, Hesketh Park, Churchtown (PR9), Marshside and the wider PR8 are all covered at the same fixed rates.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">VICTORIAN</span>&nbsp; Do you work on the Lord Street Victorian properties?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The Lord Street buildings are 130 to 170 years old. Most have been converted to flats and shops with mixed-era plumbing. Original lead supply, Victorian cast iron, 1970s upgrades, 2010s push-fit all in the same building. We work it out before we quote.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-green">RENTALS</span>&nbsp; Do you cover landlord rentals in Southport?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. The Lord Street area has high private rental and lots of HMO conversions. We cover landlord call-outs 24/7. CP12 gas safety paperwork from £80. Batch pricing for landlords with rentals across Sefton.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-navy">GAS SAFE</span>&nbsp; Are your engineers Gas Safe registered?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. All gas work is done by our own Gas Safe engineers. Check our entry at <a href="https://www.gassaferegister.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gassaferegister.co.uk</a>. It's against the law to work on gas without it.</p></div></details>
        <details class="pf-faq-item"><summary><span class="pf-faq-tag pf-tag-orange">GUARANTEE</span>&nbsp; Do you guarantee your work?</summary><div class="pf-faq-body"><p>Yes. Every job has a 12-month workmanship guarantee. If something we fixed fails because of our work, we come back. No charge.</p></div></details>
